Sprint 23 Phase A: CacheClass foundation for language package managers

Implements Phase A of docs/plans/2026-09-21-language-package-managers.md:
cache-class infrastructure so npm/pip/crates artifacts can later get TTL
metadata revalidation, verify-on-serve, and class-aware retention without
changing distro traffic behavior.

monopsony-common:
- CacheClass enum (Distro | LangArtifact) with serde snake_case
- LanguageArtifactConfig ([cache.language_artifacts]) with manual
  Default impl (non-zero numeric defaults; derive would zero them)
- UrlPattern.cache_class: Option<CacheClass> (optional; new() callers
  unaffected)

monopsony-proxy:
- StorageMeta/ObjectMeta/CacheEntry/CacheMissConfig carry cache_class;
  serde defaults keep pre-Sprint-23 sidecars loading as "distro"
- SpoolHandle.set_cache_class(): tee stamps class pre-commit so the
  .meta/ sidecar records it; sidecar now written on spool commit
- language_artifacts.rs: TTL freshness gate with origin conditional
  revalidation (ETag/If-Modified-Since), serve-stale on origin failure,
  verify-on-serve (sha256 of cached blob vs stored checksum; mismatch
  quarantines via tamper_alerts and refuses with 403)
- HIT path: quarantine check -> freshness -> verify-on-serve -> range
  stream; X-Cache: HIT|STALE reflects freshness outcome

monopsony-db:
- cache_entries.cache_class column (CREATE + idempotent ALTER)
- language_pms server_settings helpers + LanguagePmState
- record_cache_miss persists cache_class

monopsony-server:
- [cache.language_artifacts] section parsed and threaded through
  run_proxy into ProxyState

Tests: 7 new lib tests (sidecar backward compat, TTL branches,
serve-stale state preservation, verify-on-serve pass/corrupt/skip);
proxy suite 126 lib + 14 integration green; workspace check clean.

TODO(later phases): npm/pip/crates backends (B-D), scrubber + retention
floors (E, last_verified_at + audit table already in place), admin API
endpoints (F, DB helpers in place).
